Deliberate break: the georeferencing uses the nearest pose instead of interpolating
between the two that bracket the sample time (ros2_ws/src/sensor_bridge/.../georeference.py).

Expected: the unit tests go red: the interpolation and clock-offset tests of
tests/unit/test_georeference.py (samples off by up to speed x 10 ms = 1 cm against a
1 mm tolerance), and the per-sample position tests. The flight test is not expected to
catch it: with 50 Hz poses the nearest-pose error is uniform within +-10 ms x speed, so
its mean (the clock-shift rule) stays near 0 and the marker error (at most 1 cm) is far
inside the 10 cm tolerance. That is why the unit layer exists.

